{title: Shangri-La}
{artist: Traditional}
{composer: Collected by Frank Harford, 1907}
{key: D}
{tempo: 96}
{lyrics_rights: public-domain}
{genre: Traditional, Folk}
{source: Traditional. Collected by Frank Harford (1907).}
{start_of_verse}
In the years [D]when I was young
[A]Er, ah, my [D]father often [G]told me
[E]Seven long [A]years and [D]seven long [G]years
[D]I would not be [A]free
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus}
In [D]Shangri-La, [A]ah
In [D]Shangri-La, [A]ah
From [G]now on [D]you shall [A]wear
A [D]Wonderful [G]hooded [A]robe
[D]Shangri-La [G]robe
{end_of_chorus}
